CHAPTER XII
INVESTIGATION
Article 28
(1) In addition to general investigation officials, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation may also be conducted by Civil Servant Investigators whose appointment is in accordance with the laws and regulations.
(2) Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1), have the authority to:
a. receive reports or complaints from a person regarding the existence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct examination;
c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identity;
d. seize objects and/or documents; e. take fingerprints and photograph a person;
f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in expert witnesses required in connection with the examination of the case;
- 18 -
h. terminate the investigation after receiving instruction from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the public prosecutor, suspect or their family; and/or
i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
(3) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (2), shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through the Police Officer Investigator of the Republic of Indonesia Police, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

Article 11
(1) The organizational structure of P2TP2A consists of:
a. Protector/Patron;
b. Advisor;
c. Coordinator;
d. Chairperson;
e. Vice Chairperson;
f. Secretary;
g. Vice Secretary;
h. Treasurer; and
i. Members.
(2) Coordinators consist of:
a. Accompaniment and Advocacy Division;
b. Service and Recovery Division;
c. Network and Information Strengthening Division;
d. Education and Training Division;
e. Case Manager; and
f. Expert Team.
(3) Further provisions regarding the organizational structure of P2TP2A and the description of coordinator duties shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

